// ===== LEADING WHEN NOT RESPECTED, WHEN WORDS HURT, WHY WE PEOPLE-PLEASE, BRAIN DETOX & SEEING PEOPLE WHOLE, NEUROPLASTICITY & BRAIN AREAS =====
// plus data for the interactive tools: response simulator, self-checks, 30-day brain reset, brain-areas explorer
// (appended after deep.js so existing translations keep their places)

// ---------- leading when people don't respect, value or follow you ----------
PX('leadsecure','Lead From Security, Not Approval','daily','5 min','When people don\'t value or obey you, it shakes your sense of worth. Settle who you are in God first, so you can lead calmly instead of reacting.',
'Notice the sting: "I feel disrespected, ignored or small";Say: "My worth comes from God, not from their response";Separate the person from the problem: what exactly is not happening?;Ask God for wisdom about the next right step;Decide one calm action instead of a reaction',
'I keep replaying what they said => Write it down once, then set it aside until your planned conversation;I want to prove I\'m in charge => Insecure leaders demand, secure leaders serve and set clear expectations;I feel like giving up => Talk to a mentor; every leader faces this',
'Disrespect triggers the brain\'s social-threat system, the same alarm as physical danger. When worth is settled, the prefrontal cortex stays online and you can respond with wisdom rather than defend your ego.',null,
'When people don\'t listen to you, remember God loves you and made you a leader. Then you can stay calm and choose wisely.');
PX('respectconv','The Respect Conversation','deep','20–30 min','Address disrespect or disobedience directly, privately and clearly, the way Jesus taught.',
'Meet privately and at a calm time, not in front of others;Describe the specific behaviour and its effect: "When you…, it…";Ask their side and listen: "Help me understand what\'s going on";Agree on a clear expectation and the next step;Follow up kindly, and if nothing changes, involve one or two others or the proper process',
'They get defensive => Lower your voice, slow down and return to the facts;I can\'t stay calm => Do a Five-Second Pause first, or postpone the meeting;They are senior to me or my elder => Ask for a private conversation with honour and humility',
'Specific, private feedback reduces shame and defensiveness, so the other person\'s thinking brain can engage. Clear expectations remove guessing, which is a common cause of what looks like disrespect.',{min:20},
'If someone doesn\'t listen to you, talk to them alone, kindly and clearly. Tell them what you need and listen to them too.');
PX('servelead','Lead Like Jesus: Serve First','daily','10 min','Respect that lasts is earned by serving, not demanded by position. Look for one way to serve the people you lead.',
'List the people you lead: family, team, ministry or class;Ask: "What does each one need from me to grow?";Do one act of service, encouragement or help today;Admit one mistake to your team, if you made one;Thank someone publicly for their good work',
'Serving feels like weakness => Jesus washed feet and still had full authority;They take advantage => Serving is not the same as having no standards; keep clear expectations;I am too busy => Ten minutes of attention can change a relationship',
'People follow leaders they trust. Trust is built through care, consistency and humility, which calm others\' threat responses and make cooperation feel safe.',{min:10},
'A good leader helps the people they lead, like Jesus did. People follow leaders who care about them.');

// ---------- when someone insults, scolds or harms you ----------
PX('threer','When Words Hit: Regulate, Reflect, Respond','now','2–5 min','When someone uses hurtful words or scolds you, take three steps before you answer.',
'Regulate: breathe out slowly and relax your shoulders and jaw;Reflect: ask "Is there any truth here I need to hear? What is theirs to carry?";Respond: choose a calm sentence, such as "I want to talk, but not like this";If it continues, step away: "I\'ll come back when we can speak respectfully";Later, process the hurt with God and a safe person',
'I freeze and can\'t speak => Prepare one sentence ahead of time and practise it;I explode back => Leave the room first and do the Physiological Sigh;The words keep replaying => Write them down and ask, "Is this true about me?"',
'Hurtful words fire the amygdala and stress hormones within a second. Regulating first brings the thinking brain back, so you can choose a response that protects both your dignity and the relationship.',null,
'When someone says mean words, breathe first, think, then answer calmly. You don\'t have to be mean back.');
PX('blessback','Bless, Don\'t Curse Back','daily','5 min','Break the cycle of insult by choosing blessing, which frees your heart without approving the wrong.',
'Name the person and what they said or did;Tell God honestly how it made you feel;Pray one sentence of blessing for them, even if your feelings don\'t agree yet;Decide on any boundary you need;Repeat each day until bitterness loosens its grip',
'It feels fake => Blessing is a choice of the will first; feelings follow later;Blessing them means I\'m letting them off => God is the judge; blessing frees you, it does not excuse them;They are dangerous => Bless from a distance and keep yourself safe',
'Rehearsing an insult strengthens resentment circuits and keeps stress hormones high. Choosing a blessing interrupts rumination and shifts the brain toward calm and empathy.',null,
'When someone hurts you, ask God to bless them. It helps your heart get free from anger.');
PX('safetyfirst','When Words Become Harm: Safety First','deep','30 min','Insults are painful, but threats, violence, control or repeated abuse are harm. Your safety comes first.',
'Name it honestly: is this a one-off hurt, or a pattern of fear, control, threats or violence?;Tell one trusted person what is happening;Make a simple safety plan: a safe place, important numbers and a bag if needed;Get help: a counsellor, pastor, women\'s or child helpline, or the police if you are in danger;Keep records of what happens, safely',
'People say I should just forgive and stay => Forgiveness does not mean staying in danger; God protects the oppressed;I feel it is my fault => Abuse is the abuser\'s choice, never the victim\'s fault;I have nowhere to go => Call a helpline; in India dial 112 for emergencies or 181 for the women\'s helpline',
'Ongoing abuse keeps the body in survival mode and can cause trauma symptoms. Safety and support are the first steps that let the nervous system begin to heal.',{min:30},
'If someone keeps hurting you or makes you afraid, that is not okay. Tell a safe adult or call for help. It is not your fault.');

// ---------- why we people-please ----------
PX('fearyes','Find the Fear Behind the Yes','now','3 min','Before saying yes, pause and ask what is really driving it: love or fear.',
'When someone asks you for something, say "Let me check and get back to you";Ask: "Do I want to do this, or am I afraid of what will happen if I say no?";Name the fear: rejection, anger, guilt, being seen as unspiritual;Ask: "What would love, for them and for me, do here?";Answer with a clear yes or a kind no',
'I say yes before I can think => Practise the "Let me check" sentence until it is automatic;I feel guilty saying no => Guilt is a feeling, not proof you did wrong;They will be upset => Their feelings are real, but you are not responsible for managing them',
'People-pleasing is often the fawn response, a learned survival strategy that calms threat by keeping others happy. Pausing gives the prefrontal cortex time to choose instead of the old automatic reflex.',null,
'Before you say yes, stop and ask: "Am I saying yes because I love them, or because I am scared?" Then choose.');
PX('needsaudit','Your Needs Count Too','deep','15 min','Many people-pleasers have learned that their needs don\'t matter. Look honestly at what you need.',
'Draw four boxes: body, mind, relationships, faith;In each box write what you need and how often you get it;Circle the most neglected need;Plan one small way to meet it this week;Tell one person about your plan',
'It feels selfish => Jesus rested, withdrew and received care; loving your neighbour "as yourself" assumes self-care;I don\'t know what I need => Notice what drains you and what refills you;Others need me too much => Your limits are part of God\'s design, not a failure',
'Chronic self-neglect leads to exhaustion, resentment and burnout. Meeting basic needs restores energy and makes giving to others sustainable and genuine.',{min:15},
'You matter too. Taking care of your body and heart is not selfish. It helps you love others well.');
PX('resentsignal','The Resentment Signal','now','3 min','Resentment is a warning light that you have said yes when you meant no. Use it to reset your boundaries.',
'Notice resentment: irritation, complaining inside, feeling used;Ask: "Where did I agree to something I didn\'t want?";Name the need or limit you ignored;Decide what you will say next time;If needed, go back and renegotiate kindly',
'I feel resentful at everyone => You may be exhausted; start by resting;Going back on my word feels wrong => You can honour a commitment and still change future ones;I feel guilty about resentment => It is a signal, not a sin; use it wisely',
'Resentment builds when our limits are crossed repeatedly. Noticing it early activates self-awareness and helps you act before it turns into bitterness or burnout.',null,
'If you feel cross because you always help, it may mean you need to say no sometimes. That is okay.');

// ---------- brain detox and seeing people whole ----------
PX('brainreset','The 30-Day Brain Reset','deep','15 min a day','Lower the constant high stimulation of phones, porn, gaming and sugar for 30 days, so your brain can enjoy ordinary good things again.',
'Choose the high-stimulation habits you want to reduce: endless scrolling, porn, gaming, binge-watching, junk food;Set clear limits for 30 days and remove easy access;Replace them with slower rewards: walks, real conversations, reading, prayer, sport, creative work;Expect the first one to two weeks to feel restless and flat, as your brain adjusts;Track each day in the 30-Day Brain Reset tool and reflect weekly',
'I feel bored and restless => That is the adjustment; boredom often comes before creativity;I slipped on day 9 => Keep going; the days you did still count;I need my phone for work => Set app limits, use grayscale and keep it out of the bedroom',
'Very intense, constant rewards make the brain less sensitive to normal pleasures. Reducing them for a few weeks lets reward sensitivity recover, so prayer, people and nature feel rewarding again. "Dopamine detox" is a popular name; you are not removing dopamine, you are resetting how strongly your brain chases quick hits.',{min:15},
'Phones, games and other strong things can make normal fun feel boring. Take a break for 30 days and your brain will enjoy simple good things again.');
PX('seewhole','See the Whole Person','now','1 min','When your mind sexualises someone, turn your eyes and your thoughts toward seeing them as a whole person made in God\'s image.',
'Notice the moment your attention moves to someone\'s body;Turn your eyes away gently, without panic or shame;Remind yourself: "This is a person with a story, made in God\'s image, someone\'s daughter or son";Pray one short blessing for their life;Return your attention to what you were doing',
'The thoughts keep coming => Thoughts are not sins; what matters is what you do next;I feel ashamed every time => Shame feeds the cycle; respond with calm and grace;Certain places trigger me => Plan ahead and reduce your exposure',
'Repeated sexualised images train attention to scan bodies automatically. Each time you redirect attention and see the whole person, you weaken that pathway and strengthen a new, honouring one.',null,
'If you start to look at someone in the wrong way, look away and remember they are a person God loves. Say a little prayer for them.');
PX('cleaninputs','Clean Your Inputs','deep','20 min','Your brain becomes what it repeatedly takes in. Audit what you watch, follow and listen to.',
'List the apps, accounts, shows and music you consume most;Mark each one: builds me up, neutral, or pulls me down;Unfollow, mute or delete three that pull you down;Add three that feed you: Scripture, good teaching, nature, learning;Set your phone home screen to show only helpful apps',
'Everything is a bit of both => Notice how you feel after using it, not during;Friends share bad content => Mute group chats or tell them kindly;I miss what I deleted => Cravings fade within a few weeks',
'Neurons that fire together wire together. Repeated inputs shape attention, mood and desire, so changing inputs is one of the simplest ways to change the brain over time.',{min:20},
'What you watch and listen to changes your brain. Choose good things, like a healthy meal for your mind.');

// ---------- neuroplasticity and brain areas ----------
PX('speakout','Speak Truth Out Loud','daily','3 min','Saying truth aloud uses more of your brain than thinking it silently: speech, hearing and memory all work together.',
'Choose one true sentence or verse for today;Say it out loud slowly, three times;Say it once while walking or moving;Write it down by hand;Say it again before sleep',
'I feel silly => Do it in the car, shower or on a walk;My mind wanders => Shorten the sentence;I don\'t believe it yet => Say "God says…" in front of it',
'Speaking engages Broca\'s area (speech production), hearing your own voice engages the auditory cortex and Wernicke\'s area, and repetition strengthens memory. Using several pathways at once helps new beliefs stick.',{min:3},
'Say good and true words out loud. When you say them and hear them, your brain remembers them better.');
PX('learnnew','Grow New Connections: Learn Something New','deep','20–30 min','Learning a new skill, language or instrument builds new brain connections at any age.',
'Choose one new skill: a language, an instrument, drawing, a sport or a craft;Practise for 15 to 20 minutes, a few times a week;Focus on what is just a little too hard for you;Sleep well after practice so your brain can store it;Notice your progress after a month',
'I am too old => Adult brains keep forming connections throughout life;I get frustrated => Struggle is the signal that your brain is changing;I have no time => Ten focused minutes beats an hour of distraction',
'Focused practice on a new skill strengthens synapses, grows myelin and can even increase grey matter in the areas used. Effort, attention and sleep are the three ingredients of neuroplasticity.',{min:20},
'When you learn something new, your brain grows new paths, like making a new road. You can learn at any age.');
PX('handwrite','Write It by Hand','daily','5 min','Writing by hand engages more of the brain than typing and helps you remember and process.',
'Take paper and a pen;Write one thing you are learning, praying or feeling;Write slowly in your own words;Read it aloud;Keep the page where you will see it',
'My handwriting is bad => No one else needs to read it;I prefer my phone => Try paper for one week and compare;I don\'t know what to write => Copy one verse and add one sentence of your own',
'Handwriting involves motor, visual and language areas together, and studies suggest it strengthens learning and memory more than typing for many people.',{min:5},
'Writing with a pen helps your brain remember and understand better.');

