 safetyfirst:['Safety is the foundation for healing.','God defends the oppressed. Even Jesus walked away from those trying to harm Him, and Paul used his legal rights.','Psalm 9:9|The LORD also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble.','Luke 4:29-30; Acts 22:25; Proverbs 22:3','Tell one trusted person if someone is harming you.'],
 fearyes:['A pause lets you choose instead of reacting from fear.','God frees us from the fear of people so we can love freely.','Proverbs 29:25|The fear of man bringeth a snare: but whoso putteth his trust in the LORD shall be safe.','Galatians 1:10; John 12:42-43; Mark 1:35-38','Say "Let me check and get back to you" once today.'],
 needsaudit:['Meeting needs restores energy for real love.','God designed us with limits and needs. Jesus rested and received care.','Mark 6:31|Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while.','Mark 12:31; 1 Kings 19:5-8; Psalm 127:2','Meet one neglected need this week.'],
 resentsignal:['Noticing resentment early prevents bitterness.','God wants our giving to be free and cheerful, not forced.','2 Corinthians 9:7|Every man according as he purposeth in his heart, so let him give; not grudgingly, or of necessity.','Hebrews 12:15; Galatians 6:4-5; Matthew 5:37','Notice one resentment and the limit behind it.'],
