// ---------- everyday struggles ----------
DX('disrespected','My team, family or church doesn\'t respect or follow me','Work & life','leader disrespect ignore obey respect team manager staff pastor parent authority rebel',
'When people ignore, mock or resist your leadership, it hits deep: it can feel like a threat to your worth. Often the cause is a mix of unclear expectations, broken trust, the other person\'s own struggles and our insecurity.',
'Breathe out slowly before you react;Say: "My worth is not on trial"',
'Write down exactly what is happening, without exaggerating;Plan a private respect conversation',
'Serve, listen and build trust;Set clear expectations and fair consequences;Ask a mentor for honest feedback on your leadership',
'I lead from God\'s approval, not theirs.','Need for Approval;Righteous Anger vs. Ego-Driven Anger;Back-Talk and Disrespect','leadsecure;respectconv;servelead',
'When people don\'t listen to you as a leader, stay calm, talk to them kindly and alone, and keep serving them.',
['Disrespect activates the social-threat system; a secure identity and clear expectations keep you calm and fair.','Moses, David, Nehemiah and Jesus all faced people who resisted them, and God guided them.','Numbers 12:3|Now the man Moses was very meek, above all the men which were upon the face of the earth.','Nehemiah 4:14; 1 Samuel 24:6; Mark 10:42-45','Write one clear expectation and share it kindly.'],'anchor');
DX('insulted','Someone insulted, scolded or shouted at me','Relating','insult scold shout bad words abuse rude criticism humiliated yelled cursed',
'Harsh words hurt the brain much like physical pain. They can trigger shame, anger or freezing, and replay in your mind for days.',
'Breathe out slowly and loosen your jaw;Say silently: "Their words are not my identity"',
'Ask: "Is there any truth I need to hear?";Talk to a safe person about it',
'Practise a calm response sentence;Set a boundary if it keeps happening;Pray blessing, and get help if it is abuse',
'Their words say more about their pain than my worth.','Accused or shamed in a group chat;Revenge vs. Boundaries vs. Retribution vs. Restoration;Personal Boundaries','threer;blessback;safetyfirst',
'When someone says mean things to you, breathe, remember God loves you, and don\'t say mean things back. Tell someone safe.',
['Social pain uses some of the same circuits as physical pain; calming, reframing and boundaries help the brain recover.','Jesus was insulted yet did not retaliate. He entrusted Himself to the Father.','Matthew 5:11|Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you... for my sake.','1 Peter 2:23; Romans 12:17-21; Proverbs 12:16','Prepare one calm sentence for next time.'],'arrows');
DX('pleasing','I always put everyone else first and lose myself','Self','people pleaser self sacrifice cannot say no fear rejection guilt doormat overcommitted exhausted',
'People-pleasing often grows from fear: of rejection, conflict, anger or not being "good enough". It can come from a childhood where love felt conditional, or from a mistaken idea that a good Christian never says no.',
'Breathe out slowly;Say "Let me check and get back to you"',
'Find the fear behind one yes today;Do one small thing for your own needs',
'Practise one small, kind no each week;Notice resentment as a signal;Rest your worth in God\'s love, not others\' approval',
'I can love people without losing myself.','People-Pleasing;Fawn Response;The People-Pleasing Mask','fearyes;needsaudit;resentsignal',
'If you always do what others want and forget yourself, you might be scared of upsetting them. God loves you, and it\'s okay to say no sometimes.',
['The fawn response keeps the threat system calm by pleasing others; safety in God\'s love lets the brain choose freely.','Jesus loved deeply but also said no, withdrew and rested. He was secure in the Father\'s approval.','Galatians 1:10|For do I now persuade men, or God? or do I seek to please men?','Mark 1:35-38; John 12:43; Proverbs 29:25','Say one kind no this week.'],'coach');
DX('overstim','My brain feels overstimulated and craves quick hits','Mind','overstimulated dopamine addicted phone porn gaming bored restless brain fog detox',
'Constant scrolling, games, porn and sugar flood the reward system, so normal life feels dull. Concentration drops, boredom feels unbearable and cravings grow.',
'Put your phone in another room;Take a short walk outside',
'Remove one quick-hit app for a day;Do one slow, real-world activity',
'Start the 30-Day Brain Reset;Clean your inputs;Build daily habits of prayer, movement and real connection',
'My brain can learn to enjoy simple good things again.','The Reward Loop: Dopamine & Habits;Doomscrolling and phone urges;Breaking a bad habit','brainreset;cleaninputs;seewhole',
'If your brain always wants your phone or games, take a break. After a while, simple things will feel fun again.',
['High-stimulation habits reduce reward sensitivity; a reset lets the brain recover its natural balance.','God invites us to fast, rest and set our minds on what is good.','Psalm 119:37|Turn away mine eyes from beholding vanity; and quicken thou me in thy way.','1 Corinthians 6:12; Philippians 4:8; Isaiah 55:2','Start day one of the brain reset today.'],'garden');
DX('sexthoughts','Sexual thoughts keep popping into my mind','Mind','sexual thoughts lust intrusive images porn memories fantasy mind',
'After exposure to porn or sexualised media, the brain can keep replaying images and scanning for them. Fighting thoughts with panic often makes them louder.',
'Notice the thought without panic;Turn your eyes and attention to something in front of you',
'See the whole person and bless them;Reduce the triggers in your inputs',
'Keep a steady brain reset;Talk to a safe person or counsellor;Fill your mind with good, beautiful and true things',
'A thought is not a sin. I can turn my attention and heal.','Unwanted sexual behaviour (pornography, fantasy, secret habits);The Habit Loop;Grace vs. Shame','seewhole;brainreset;cleaninputs',
'If bad pictures pop into your mind, don\'t panic. Look at something else and think about good things. Your brain can heal.',
['Redirecting attention calmly weakens the old pathway; panic and shame strengthen it.','God renews our minds and invites us to think on what is pure.','Philippians 4:8|Whatsoever things are pure... think on these things.','2 Corinthians 10:5; Job 31:1; Romans 12:2','Choose one verse to turn to when a thought comes.'],'lens');

